(14):(["$ gym score --now 1760086522000\nscoreboard from 4 logged attempts; only delayed, unassisted and held-out results count\nretention: not enough data (n = 1, need 5)\n  Of the attempts on items you had last tried at least a day earlier, with no hints and no tap-out, the share you got right. It shows what stuck after a delay.\ntransfer: not enough data (n = 0, need 5)\n  The share you got right on held-out items that are never used in practice, so the number cannot come from memorising answers.\ncalibration: not enough data (n = 3, need 5)\n  The Brier score of your confidence on the first attempt at each item: 0 is perfect, 0.25 is what saying 50 percent every time earns, 1 is always certain and always wrong. Lower is better.\nindependence: not enough data (n = 4, need 5)\n  Hints used plus tap-outs, for each item you solved. Lower is better; a falling trend shows the scaffolding fading.\nfluency: not enough data (n = 2, need 5)\n  The median seconds you took on answers that were right with no hints and no tap-out. A falling number shows the skill becoming automatic.\nsynthesis: not enough data (n = 0, need 5)\n  The share you got right, with no hint and no tap-out, on synthesis items: questions that combine ideas from different parts of the subject. It shows whether separate pieces of knowledge have joined up.\n[exit 0; log 1514 -> 1514 bytes]", "0"])
